{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ASvwmbMhFMHzad6FfGaaEf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 SciERC 上 zero-shot 最小提示下的 ontology violation 基准测试\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_triples\": 1724,\n7\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.154,\n8\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.014,\n9\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n10\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n11\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n12\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.01\n13\t    },\n14\t    \"tables\": [\n15\t      \"Table 1: SciERC Phase 0 per-relation violation rates (7 relations). Reviewer 标注：'3 relations drive all violations — this is a data sparsity issue, not a systematic phenomenon'\"\n16\t    ],\n17\t    \"figures\": [],\n18\t    \"analysis\": \"审稿人将 violation landscape 从 \\\"systematic phenomenon\\\" 降级为 \\\"long-tail artifact on a small ontology\\\"。 核心攻击：SciERC 只有 7 relations，violation 集中在 3 个关系上，不足以证明 \\\"LLM IE 系统性地违反 ontology constraints\\\"。 Path A reframe 下可辩护：即使集中在 3 个关系，这些关系的 25-42% violation rate 仍对下游系统产生不可忽视影响。 但需要补充更多 ontology 的 violation landscape 数据才能说服审稿人。\\n\\n\\n数据本身无变化。worst 档下审稿人攻击角度：(1) \\\"15.4% DR on a 7-relation ontology is expected — with only 6 entity types and loose constraints on Used-for (787 triples, 0.76%), the violation rate is inflated by 3 specific relations (Feature-of/Compare/Evaluate-for) that account for 85%+ of violations. This is a long-tail artifact, not a systemic problem.\\\" (2) \\\"R-F1=8.23% 说明模型根本没有学到任务结构， 在一个模型基本不会做的任务上测 violation rate 有什么意义？\\\" (3) 2-3 位审稿人认为 SciERC violation landscape 是 \\\"useful but incremental observation\\\"，不足以支撑独立 contribution。\\n\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n22\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 SciERC 上 schema-informed prompting 后的 violation 变化\",\n23\t    \"results\": {\n24\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.058,\n25\t      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -62.4,\n26\t      \"total_triples\": 1661,\n27\t      \"evaluate_for_dr_delta_pp\": 5.8,\n28\t      \"feature_of_dr_delta_pp\": -22.3,\n29\t      \"compare_dr_delta_pp\": -14.8\n30\t    },\n31\t    \"tables\": [\n32\t      \"Table 2: Schema-informed vs minimal per-relation DR delta. Reviewer 圈出：'5/7 relations improve — this is a reasonable success rate for zero-cost intervention'\"\n33\t    ],\n34\t    \"figures\": [],\n35\t    \"analysis\": \"\\\"Prompt insufficiency\\\" claim 在 worst 档下被判定 undersupported——审稿人要求至少 3 种 prompting strategy (minimal / schema-informed / few-shot / CoT) 的对比才能声称 \\\"prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable\\\"。 单一 schema-informed prompt 的 62% reduction 反而被用来论证 \\\"prompting works pretty well\\\"。 Path B reframe 可规避：不声称 prompt insufficient，而是将 prompt 定位为 trade-off space 的一个点。\\n\\n\\nworst 档审稿人攻击：(1) \\\"62.4% reduction with just prompting — the problem is largely solvable without constrained decoding. The residual 5.78% could be addressed by better prompt engineering (few-shot, chain-of-thought) rather than building a complex decoding framework.\\\" (2) Evaluate-for regression (+5.8pp) 被 1 位审稿人标记但未被多数视为 critical—— 更致命的是另一角度：\\\"you tested ONE prompting strategy; claiming 'prompt insufficiency' without trying few-shot / CoT / self-consistency is premature.\\\" (3) McNemar test significance 不足以挽回—— 审稿人关注的是 \\\"是否穷尽了 prompt 方案\\\" 而非 \\\"当前方案是否 significant\\\"。\\n\"\n36\t  },\n37\t  {\n38\t    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n39\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 DocRED (96 relations) 上 zero-shot 最小提示下的 violation 基准\",\n40\t    \"results\": {\n41\t      \"total_triples\": 16540,\n42\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.187,\n43\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.289,\n44\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.075,\n45\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.964\n46\t    },\n47\t    \"tables\": [\n48\t      \"Table 3: DocRED Phase 0 top violations by count/rate. Reviewer：'P31_instance_of DR=60.4% with 533 triples — this single relation type drives the narrative'\"\n49\t    ],\n50\t    \"figures\": [],\n51\t    \"analysis\": \"审稿人攻击核心：在 zero-shot R-F1 < 10% 的 setting 下，violation pattern 的外部效度存疑。 \\\"You're characterizing the error patterns of a system that doesn't work\\\" 是最致命的一句。 这直接威胁 C1 (violation landscape) 作为独立贡献的可信度。Path A reframe 需要在论文中前置 \\\"we study violation patterns as a function of ontology structure, not model capability\\\" 的定位， 但审稿人可能仍不买账。\\n\\n\\nworst 档审稿人关注点转移：(1) \\\"RV=28.9% means nearly 1/3 of predicted relations are OOV — the model is barely following instructions. Measuring DR on a system that can't even produce valid relation names is questionable methodology.\\\" (2) \\\"ET=7.5% further confirms the model is struggling with basic task understanding in zero-shot DocRED. Your violation landscape is measuring noise, not systematic behavior.\\\" (3) 1 位审稿人直接质疑：\\\"with 96 relations and no training data, this is a toy evaluation that tells us nothing about how real IE systems would behave.\\\" 核心问题： zero-shot F1 太低 → 审稿人不信 violation pattern 反映真实 IE 系统行为。\\n\"\n52\t  },\n53\t  {\n54\t    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n55\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 DocRED 上 schema-informed prompting 后的 violation 变化\",\n56\t    \"results\": {\n57\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n58\t      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -32,\n59\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.945,\n60\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.184\n61\t    },\n62\t    \"tables\": [\n63\t      \"Table 4: SciERC vs DocRED prompt effect comparison. Reviewer：'the gap (62% vs 32%) could simply reflect prompt sensitivity to ontology size, not a fundamental limitation'\"\n64\t    ],\n65\t    \"figures\": [],\n66\t    \"analysis\": \"32% vs 62% 的 gap 本意支持 \\\"prompt scales poorly\\\" claim，但审稿人反转论证为 \\\"这说明 zero-shot 96-relation 任务太难，不是一个合理的 evaluation setting\\\"。 核心矛盾：作者需要 DocRED 来展示 ontology complexity effect，但 zero-shot DocRED 的质量太低导致审稿人质疑整个 evaluation framework。\\n\\n\\n审稿人攻击点：(1) \\\"Only 32% DR reduction (vs SciERC 62%) — schema-informed prompting degrades with ontology complexity. But wait, you claim this SUPPORTS your method. If prompting scales poorly, surely constrained decoding will also face scalability challenges with 96 relations?\\\" (2) \\\"RV 只从 28.9% 降到 18.4%——prompting 甚至不能解决 OOV 问题，说明模型在 DocRED 上 根本不遵循 instructions。这是模型问题，不是 prompting vs decoding 问题。\\\" (3) parse rate 从 96.4% 降到 94.5%——\\\"prompting actually made parsing slightly worse。\\\" 审稿人用这组数据论证 \\\"zero-shot DocRED 太难，方法无法在此 setting 下有效评估\\\"。\\n\"\n67\t  },\n68\t  {\n69\t    \"name\": \"SciERC unconstrained baseline\",\n70\t    \"description\": \"Phase 2 SciERC unconstrained 基准（与 Phase 0 一致性验证）\",\n71\t    \"results\": {\n72\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.154,\n73\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.014,\n74\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n75\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n76\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n77\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.01,\n78\t      \"total_triples\": 1724\n79\t    },\n80\t    \"tables\": [\n81\t      \"Table 5: SciERC ablation matrix (5 configs). Reviewer 在 header 批注：'All R-F1 < 9% — these results are within noise'\"\n82\t    ],\n83\t    \"figures\": [],\n84\t    \"analysis\": \"基准实验本身无问题。审稿人利用低绝对 F1 质疑整个实验矩阵的信息量。 \\\"You've shown your method works on bad predictions. Who cares?\\\" 是最简洁的攻击。\\n\\n\\n基准数字与 P001 一致，确认 Phase 2 pipeline 可复现。worst 档下审稿人不攻击一致性， 而是攻击 baseline 本身：\\\"R-F1=8.23% — the model is essentially random. Evaluating constraint enforcement on random-quality output is methodologically questionable.\\\" 这个攻击贯穿所有后续 SciERC 实验——审稿人认为低 F1 下的 violation reduction 没有实际意义。\\n\"\n85\t  },\n86\t  {\n87\t    \"name\": \"SciERC grammar-only\",\n88\t    \"description\": \"仅 grammar 层（XGrammar CFG）约束下的 SciERC 结果\",\n89\t    \"results\": {\n90\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.148,\n91\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n92\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n93\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n94\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n95\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 30.98\n96\t    },\n97\t    \"tables\": [],\n98\t    \"figures\": [],\n99\t    \"analysis\": \"Grammar-only 的作用（消除 RV/ET）被审稿人最小化——\\\"this is standard XGrammar application, not a contribution\\\"。同时 grammar-only DR≈unconstrained 成为审稿人论证 \\\"grammar 层 对核心 violation 类型无效\\\" 的证据。在 worst 档下，grammar 层的正面贡献（enabling semantic） 被忽视，只看到 \\\"grammar alone doesn't solve DR\\\"。\\n\\n\\nGrammar 层消除 RV 和 ET 但不影响 DR（14.84% ≈ 15.37%），符合预期——CFG 无法表达 cross-field 约束。worst 档审稿人攻击：(1) \\\"Grammar-only already achieves the main practical benefit — eliminating OOV relation names and invalid entity types. The residual DR=14.84% could be addressed by post-hoc filtering without the complexity of a stateful semantic layer.\\\" (2) \\\"F1 完全不变 (8.23→8.23)——grammar 约束对 extraction quality 零影响。\\\" 审稿人论证 grammar-only 已经 \\\"good enough\\\"，semantic 层的复杂性不值得。\\n\"\n100\t  },\n101\t  {\n102\t    \"name\": \"SciERC semantic-only\",\n103\t    \"description\": \"仅 semantic 层（logit masking）约束下的 SciERC 结果\",\n104\t    \"results\": {\n105\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.117,\n106\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.015,\n107\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n108\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.027,\n109\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.15,\n110\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.01\n111\t    },\n112\t    \"tables\": [],\n113\t    \"figures\": [],\n114\t    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 是 worst 档最危险的数据点之一——它直接暴露了 \\\"如果剥离 XGrammar（已有工具）， 作者的实际贡献只有 24% DR reduction + 引入 2.7% CF\\\"。审稿人会写： \\\"The authors' genuinely novel contribution — the semantic constraint layer — achieves modest violation reduction (24%) while introducing a new type of inconsistency (CF 2.7%).\\\"\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR=11.65%（仅↓24%）——因为没有 grammar 层，遇到 OOV relation 时 semantic 无法查 constraint table，大量 token 位置约束失效。worst 档审稿人攻击： (1) \\\"Semantic-only 24% reduction vs full 94% — this shows your semantic layer is heavily dependent on grammar. But the grammar layer is just XGrammar (existing tool). So your actual novel contribution (semantic layer) only achieves 24% DR reduction on its own.\\\" (2) \\\"CF 已经从 0.08% 跳到 2.71%——semantic 层引入 CF 的同时只减少 24% DR， cost-benefit 不佳。\\\" (3) \\\"R-F1 下降 0.08pp——虽然不显著，但方向是负的。\\\" 这组数据被审稿人用来论证 \\\"核心 novelty（semantic layer）alone 效果不够\\\"。\\n\"\n115\t  },\n116\t  {\n117\t    \"name\": \"SciERC full S1\",\n118\t    \"description\": \"SciERC grammar+semantic S1 单遍完整约束\",\n119\t    \"results\": {\n120\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.009,\n121\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n122\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n123\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.099,\n124\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.36,\n125\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 30.98,\n126\t      \"total_triples\": 1729\n127\t    },\n128\t    \"tables\": [\n129\t      \"Table 5 (full ablation): Reviewer 在 full_s1 行用红笔标注 CF=9.9%，批注 'new violation introduced by method'\"\n130\t    ],\n131\t    \"figures\": [],\n132\t    \"analysis\": \"CF=9.9% 是 worst 档的核心 rejection 理由。审稿人不接受 \\\"DR=hard constraint, CF=soft preference\\\" 的分级叙事——认为这是作者为掩盖方法缺陷而设的 ad hoc 区分。\\\"Net violation improvement\\\" 视角 下效果大打折扣。Path B reframe（将 CF 升级为 core research question）可直接应对这一攻击。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.93%（↓94%）是论文核心数字。worst 档审稿人承认 DR reduction 显著，但攻击焦点 转向 CF=9.9%：(1) \\\"You traded 15.37% DR for 9.9% CF. DR violations produce structurally invalid triples; CF violations produce semantically inconsistent entity typing across relations. Both are problematic for downstream systems. The net reduction in 'problematic triples' is only ~5pp, not the claimed 94%.\\\" (2) \\\"CF=9.9% 意味着近 10% 的 entity 在不同 relation 中 被分配了不同 type——这在知识图谱中是致命的一致性问题。作者试图用 'severity distinction' (DR=hard, CF=soft) 来淡化，但这个区分是 subjective 的。\\\" (3) \\\"R-F1 从 8.23 到 8.36 (+0.13pp, p=0.58)——统计不显著，F1 claims 站不住。\\\" (4) 1-2 位审稿人直接引用 CF 数据判定 \\\"method introduces a new violation type to fix another\\\"。\\n\"\n133\t  },\n134\t  {\n135\t    \"name\": \"SciERC full S2 (ablation)\",\n136\t    \"description\": \"SciERC 两遍 S2 策略 ablation\",\n137\t    \"results\": {\n138\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.01,\n139\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n140\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n141\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.08,\n142\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.03,\n143\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.9,\n144\t      \"total_triples\": 1644,\n145\t      \"total_entities\": 2228\n146\t    },\n147\t    \"tables\": [\n148\t      \"Table 5 S2 行: Reviewer 批注 'S2 was supposed to mitigate CF — it doesn't'\"\n149\t    ],\n150\t    \"figures\": [],\n151\t    \"analysis\": \"S2 失败是 worst 档 CF narrative 的加速器。审稿人逻辑：如果连作者自己设计的 CF 缓解策略 都失败了，那 \\\"future work: global consistency pass\\\" 的承诺 credibility 极低。 这将 CF 从 \\\"acknowledged limitation with clear path forward\\\" 降级为 \\\"fundamental unresolved problem that the authors have already failed to address\\\"。\\n\\n\\nS2 设计初衷是用两遍解码缓解 CF，但实际 CF=8.03% vs S1=9.9%——差距不显著（1.87pp）。 worst 档审稿人攻击：(1) \\\"S2 adds significant complexity (two-pass decoding) for negligible CF reduction (-1.87pp). R-F1 actually drops (8.03 vs 8.36). This undermines the authors' ability to iterate on the CF problem — their own best idea for addressing CF failed.\\\" (2) \\\"S2 generates 85 fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) and 246 fewer entities (2228 vs 2474)—— two-pass decoding causes information loss.\\\" (3) \\\"如果作者自己的 S2 方案都解决不了 CF， 这说明 CF 是 per-relation enforcement 的固有缺陷，不是 'future work' 能解决的。\\\" S2 的失败强化了 CF 作为 fundamental limitation 的判定。\\n\"\n152\t  },\n153\t  {\n154\t    \"name\": \"DocRED unconstrained baseline\",\n155\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B DocRED unconstrained 基准\",\n156\t    \"results\": {\n157\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.185,\n158\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.297,\n159\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n160\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n161\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 7.74,\n162\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 58.15,\n163\t      \"total_triples\": 17497,\n164\t      \"parse_failures\": 12\n165\t    },\n166\t    \"tables\": [\n167\t      \"Table 6: DocRED ablation matrix. Reviewer 在 baseline 行标注 'RV=29.7% — model doesn't understand the task'\"\n168\t    ],\n169\t    \"figures\": [],\n170\t    \"analysis\": \"RV=29.7% 是 worst 档 DocRED 叙事的核心弱点——审稿人论证 grammar 层的 F1 提升（P010/P012） 只是将 OOV 强制映射到有效关系名，不是真正的 extraction quality 提升。 \\\"Your grammar layer is doing label correction, not constraint enforcement\\\" 是最致命的 reframing。\\n\\n\\nDocRED baseline 暴露两个 worst 档攻击面：(1) RV=29.66%——\\\"nearly 1/3 of triples use non-existent relation names. This is not a violation problem, this is a task comprehension problem. Your method's DR reduction is inflated because grammar forces OOV relations into valid names, artificially improving DR without improving extraction.\\\" (2) R-F1=7.74%—— \\\"absolute quality indistinguishable from noise on a 96-relation task.\\\" 审稿人论证 zero-shot DocRED 不是一个 meaningful evaluation setting。Entity F1=58.15% 被忽视—— \\\"entity extraction is easier, but the paper claims contributions to relation extraction.\\\"\\n\"\n171\t  },\n172\t  {\n173\t    \"name\": \"DocRED grammar-only\",\n174\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 grammar 层约束\",\n175\t    \"results\": {\n176\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.262,\n177\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n178\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n179\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n180\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.31,\n181\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 59.38,\n182\t      \"parse_failures\": 13\n183\t    },\n184\t    \"tables\": [\n185\t      \"Table 6 grammar-only 行：Reviewer 用红色标注 DR↑ 箭头：'grammar makes DR WORSE'\"\n186\t    ],\n187\t    \"figures\": [],\n188\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED grammar-only DR 上升是 worst 档最直观的攻击素材。审稿人叙事： \\\"Step 1 of your method (grammar) actively worsens the violation you claim to solve (DR). You need Step 2 (semantic) to clean up the mess Step 1 created. This is not 'composable' constraint enforcement — this is one layer creating problems for another layer to fix.\\\" 这直接挑战 \\\"complementary with enabling dependency\\\" 的技术叙事。\\n\\n\\nGrammar 消除 RV（29.66%→0.03%）和 ET（2.48%→0%），但 DR 从 18.46% 升至 26.17%—— worst 档审稿人抓住这一点：(1) \\\"Grammar INCREASES DR by 7.7pp! When you force OOV relation names into valid names, you're creating new DR violations because the forced valid name has different domain/range constraints than what the model intended. Your grammar layer actively worsens the core problem you claim to solve.\\\" (2) \\\"E-F1 提升 (+1.23pp) 来自消除 OOV entity types——this is not 'constraint enforcement improving extraction,' it's grammar fixing the model's formatting errors. Any JSON schema validator could do this.\\\" (3) \\\"DR=26.17% 是所有配置中最高的——grammar 单独使用 比不用更差。\\\" 审稿人用 grammar-only DR 上升来质疑整个 composable 框架的设计合理性。\\n\"\n189\t  },\n190\t  {\n191\t    \"name\": \"DocRED semantic-only\",\n192\t    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 semantic 层约束\",\n193\t    \"results\": {\n194\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.138,\n195\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.299,\n196\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.042,\n197\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.011,\n198\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 7.7,\n199\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 57.81\n200\t    },\n201\t    \"tables\": [],\n202\t    \"figures\": [],\n203\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED semantic-only 数据在 worst 档下被解读为 \\\"作者的核心贡献（semantic 层）在复杂 ontology 上效果有限\\\"。DR 仅降 25%、CF 开始出现、F1 略降——三面夹击。 审稿人在此处建立 \\\"method doesn't scale to complex ontologies\\\" 的论据基础。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR=13.84%（仅↓25%），RV/ET 不变——因为 semantic 层不处理 vocabulary。 worst 档审稿人用这组数据闭合论证：(1) \\\"Semantic-only reduces DR by only 25% while introducing CF=1.05%. Grammar-only increases DR by 42% while fixing RV/ET. Neither layer works well alone. The 'composable' claim is misleading — the layers are CODEPENDENT, and the codependency is fragile (see DocRED fallback rate ~57/doc).\\\" (2) \\\"E-F1 实际下降 0.34pp (57.81 vs 58.15)——semantic 层 alone 对 extraction 有害。\\\" (3) \\\"比较 semantic-only DR=13.84% 和 full_s1 DR=10.21%——加了 grammar 后 DR 只额外 降了 3.6pp。如果 grammar 层 'enables' semantic，为什么 full_s1 DR 不接近 0%？\\\"\\n\"\n204\t  },\n205\t  {\n206\t    \"name\": \"DocRED full S1\",\n207\t    \"description\": \"DocRED grammar+semantic S1 完整约束\",\n208\t    \"results\": {\n209\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.102,\n210\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n211\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n212\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.026,\n213\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n214\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 59.37,\n215\t      \"parse_failures\": 11\n216\t    },\n217\t    \"tables\": [\n218\t      \"Table 6 full_s1 行: Reviewer 批注 'DR=10.2% is far from near-complete'\",\n219\t      \"Cross-dataset comparison: SciERC DR↓94% vs DocRED DR↓45%. Reviewer：'this is a 2× degradation, not graceful scaling'\"\n220\t    ],\n221\t    \"figures\": [],\n222\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED DR↓44.7% 是 worst 档第二大 rejection driver（仅次于 CF）。审稿人叙事： \\\"The method's flagship claim — near-complete type validity — holds only on a tiny 7-relation ontology. On a realistic 96-relation ontology, 10% of triples remain invalid. Combined with CF=2.57% (new violations introduced), the net violation picture is: 10.2% DR + 2.6% CF = ~12.8% problematic triples, vs baseline 18.5% — a modest 31% net improvement, not the claimed 94%.\\\" 这个 \\\"net improvement\\\" reframing 极其危险。\\n\\n\\nDR=10.21%（↓44.7%）——远低于 SciERC 的 94%。worst 档审稿人攻击： (1) \\\"DR reduction drops from 94% (SciERC) to 45% (DocRED). The method HALVES in effectiveness on a more complex ontology. This is a critical scalability failure — real-world IE ontologies have hundreds of relation types.\\\" (2) \\\"Residual DR=10.21% — every 10th triple still violates domain/range constraints. 'Near-complete' in the title is inaccurate for DocRED.\\\" (3) \\\"Qwen DocRED DR↓44.7% 与 Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% 的巨大差距说明方法效果 高度 model-dependent，不是 ontology-agnostic 的 general solution。\\\" (4) \\\"F1 提升 (+0.50pp R-F1, p<0.001) 主要来自 grammar 消除 OOV—— grammar_only E-F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%。Semantic 层对 F1 零贡献。\\\" 审稿人合并 SciERC 94% vs DocRED 45% 为 \\\"method unreliable on complex scenarios\\\"。\\n\"\n223\t  },\n224\t  {\n225\t    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC unconstrained\",\n226\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC unconstrained 基准\",\n227\t    \"results\": {\n228\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.133,\n229\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.006,\n230\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n231\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n232\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 2.68,\n233\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 23.56,\n234\t      \"total_relations\": 1274,\n235\t      \"parse_failures\": 1\n236\t    },\n237\t    \"tables\": [\n238\t      \"Table 7: Cross-model comparison. Reviewer 标注 Llama R-F1 列：'2.68% is noise'\"\n239\t    ],\n240\t    \"figures\": [],\n241\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama SciERC baseline 暴露了 cross-model 验证的结构性弱点：两个模型在同一任务上 质量差异巨大（2.68% vs 8.23%），说明 zero-shot IE 本身不稳定。审稿人论证 \\\"if the base task quality varies 3× across models, constraint enforcement on top of it is evaluating a moving target\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLlama SciERC R-F1=2.68%——比 Qwen 的 8.23% 还低 3×。worst 档审稿人攻击： (1) \\\"R-F1=2.68% — this model extracts essentially nothing correct. Demonstrating constraint enforcement on a model with 2.68% F1 is meaningless.\\\" (2) \\\"You chose Llama specifically because it has low RV (0.55%) — this makes grammar layer look good (it has nothing to fix). But the real story is the model can't do the task.\\\" (3) \\\"E-F1=23.56% (vs Qwen 31.01%)—— Llama 在 SciERC 上全面弱于 Qwen，cross-model 'validation' 只是在一个更弱的模型上 重复了同样的实验。\\\" 审稿人认为 2 个 8B 模型 + 2 个数据集 = 最低限度验证，不足以 支撑 generalization claim。\\n\"\n242\t  },\n243\t  {\n244\t    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC full S1\",\n245\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC 完整 S1 约束\",\n246\t    \"results\": {\n247\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n248\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n249\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n250\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.066,\n251\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 2.54,\n252\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 23.49,\n253\t      \"total_relations\": 1315\n254\t    },\n255\t    \"tables\": [\n256\t      \"Table 7 Llama S1 行: Reviewer 标注 CF=6.56% + R-F1↓\"\n257\t    ],\n258\t    \"figures\": [],\n259\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama SciERC DR↓99.4% 表面极好但审稿人论证这是 \\\"easy case\\\"（低 RV baseline）。 CF=6.56% 高于 Qwen 同场景进一步支持 \\\"CF is model-dependent and unpredictable\\\" 叙事。 R-F1 下降虽小但方向不利——\\\"constrained decoding hurts already-weak models\\\" 的论点。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.08%（↓99.4%）——数字极好，但 worst 档审稿人翻转叙事： (1) \\\"DR↓99.4% on Llama vs ↓94% on Qwen — why does the method work BETTER on the weaker model? Because Llama has near-zero RV (0.55%), so grammar layer encounters fewer OOV issues and semantic layer operates more cleanly. This means your method's effectiveness depends heavily on the model's baseline vocabulary compliance, not on the method's own capability.\\\" (2) \\\"CF=6.56% — higher than Qwen's CF rate on the same dataset. Constrained decoding destabilizes Llama's entity typing more than Qwen's.\\\" (3) \\\"R-F1 从 2.68% 降到 2.54% (-0.14pp)——在已经极低的 F1 上还进一步下降。\\\" (4) \\\"Parse failure 从 1 增加到... 好吧 Llama SciERC parse failure 没增加， 但 R-F1 下降 + CF 升高 = constrained decoding hurts Llama stability。\\\"\\n\"\n260\t  },\n261\t  {\n262\t    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED unconstrained\",\n263\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED unconstrained 基准\",\n264\t    \"results\": {\n265\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.261,\n266\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.16,\n267\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n268\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n269\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 5.98,\n270\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 55.65,\n271\t      \"parse_failures\": 68,\n272\t      \"documents_checked\": 930\n273\t    },\n274\t    \"tables\": [\n275\t      \"Table 7 Llama DocRED baseline: Reviewer：'68 parse failures (6.8%) — significant selection bias'\"\n276\t    ],\n277\t    \"figures\": [],\n278\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED baseline 的 parse failure=6.8% 引入 selection bias 攻击。审稿人指出： checker 跳过 parse failures → F1 只在成功解析的 93.2% 样本上计算 → 这些样本可能 系统性地 easier/better → 所有 Llama DocRED 数字都有上偏。 虽然偏差方向对 constrained decoding 不利（见 P016 parse failure 更高）， 但审稿人可能不接受这个辩护——\\\"you should report F1 on ALL documents, with parse failures counted as zero extraction\\\"。\\n\\n\\nParse failures=68/998（6.8%）是 worst 档攻击面之一：(1) \\\"6.8% parse failure rate means the model can't even produce valid JSON 7% of the time. These failures are excluded from F1 calculation — creating a selection bias that favors the method.\\\" (2) \\\"DR=26.07% (vs Qwen 18.46%) — Llama has MORE DR violations on DocRED despite having FEWER RV violations (16.0% vs 29.7%). This contradicts the 'tightness × RV baseline' narrative — if RV explains DR reduction gap, why does Llama have higher baseline DR with lower baseline RV?\\\" 审稿人用这个不一致来质疑 D014 dual-factor 解释。 (3) \\\"R-F1=5.98% — even worse than Qwen's 7.74%. Another data point confirming zero-shot DocRED is not a meaningful evaluation setting.\\\"\\n\"\n279\t  },\n280\t  {\n281\t    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED full S1\",\n282\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED 完整 S1 约束\",\n283\t    \"results\": {\n284\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.026,\n285\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n286\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n287\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.12,\n288\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 6.27,\n289\t      \"entity_f1_pct\": 55.01,\n290\t      \"parse_failures\": 91,\n291\t      \"documents_checked\": 907\n292\t    },\n293\t    \"tables\": [\n294\t      \"Table 7 Llama DocRED S1: 被红色标注的数字 — CF=12.02%, parse_failures=91, E-F1↓0.64pp\",\n295\t      \"Cross-model CF comparison: Qwen 2.57% vs Llama 12.02%. Reviewer：'CF is 4.7× worse on Llama — this is not a stable method'\"\n296\t    ],\n297\t    \"figures\": [],\n298\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED full_s1 是 worst 档 \\\"方法不稳定\\\" 论据的核心证据。CF=12.02%、 parse_failures 增加 33.8%、E-F1 下降——三个负面指标同时出现。 审稿人叙事总结：\\\"On Llama DocRED, OntoCoDec reduces DR from 26% to 2.5% (good), but introduces CF=12% (new problem), increases parse failures by 34% (stability issue), and slightly degrades entity F1 (quality loss). The trade-off is unfavorable.\\\" 这是 ≥2 审稿人给 reject 的关键段落。\\n\\n\\nDR=2.55%（↓90.2%）——比 Qwen 的 44.7% 好得多，但 worst 档审稿人合并攻击面： (1) \\\"CF=12.02% — the highest of any configuration. One in eight entities has inconsistent typing. On DocRED this is especially problematic because the same entities appear across many relations in a document.\\\" (2) \\\"Parse failures increased from 68 to 91 (+33.8%)—— constrained decoding actively destabilizes Llama's JSON generation. 23 additional documents produced unparseable output BECAUSE of your constraints.\\\" (3) \\\"E-F1=55.01% (↓0.64pp)—— entity extraction quality dropped. This contradicts the SciERC claim of F1-neutrality.\\\" (4) \\\"Cross-model inconsistency: Qwen DR↓44.7% vs Llama DR↓90.2% (2× gap). Method effectiveness varies wildly across models — users cannot predict what reduction they'll get.\\\" (5) \\\"CF 跨模型差异更极端：Qwen CF=2.57% vs Llama CF=12.02% (4.7× gap)。 方法引入的新问题（CF）比它解决的旧问题（DR）更不可预测。\\\" 审稿人合并所有 cross-model 不一致性判定 \\\"method is unreliable\\\"。\\n\"\n299\t  },\n300\t  {\n301\t    \"name\": \"S2 pilot (50 docs)\",\n302\t    \"description\": \"S2 两遍策略 50 文档 pilot 测试\",\n303\t    \"results\": {\n304\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.021,\n305\t      \"relation_f1_pct\": 10.08,\n306\t      \"samples\": 50,\n307\t      \"predicted_relations\": 146\n308\t    },\n309\t    \"tables\": [],\n310\t    \"figures\": [],\n311\t    \"analysis\": \"Pilot50 在 worst 档下无独立攻击面，但论文必须确保无残留引用。 审稿人通常会在 Appendix 检查 pilot 数字与主表一致性。\\n\\n\\nPilot50 数据已被全量 S2（P008）supersede。worst 档审稿人会在看到论文引用 pilot50 时 检查是否与全量数据一致——pilot DR=2.05% vs full DR=0.97%，数字不一致。 如果论文任何地方残留 pilot50 数字，审稿人会标注 \\\"inconsistent reporting\\\"。 但因为 pilot 已明确标注为 superseded，主要风险是论文写作中的引用错误。\\n\"\n312\t  },\n313\t  {\n314\t    \"name\": \"Post-hoc filtering baseline\",\n315\t    \"description\": \"Post-hoc 过滤 baseline 对比（删除违规 triples）\",\n316\t    \"results\": {\n317\t      \"scierc_f1_after\": 8.63,\n318\t      \"scierc_f1_before\": 8.23,\n319\t      \"scierc_rejection_rate\": 0.168,\n320\t      \"scierc_recall_after\": 10.68,\n321\t      \"scierc_recall_before\": 11.4,\n322\t      \"scierc_tp_before\": 111,\n323\t      \"scierc_tp_after\": 104,\n324\t      \"docred_f1_after\": 9.61,\n325\t      \"docred_f1_before\": 7.74,\n326\t      \"docred_rejection_rate\": 0.481,\n327\t      \"docred_recall_after\": 8.4,\n328\t      \"docred_recall_before\": 9.46,\n329\t      \"docred_tp_before\": 1137,\n330\t      \"docred_tp_after\": 1010,\n331\t      \"docred_et_residual\": 0.025\n332\t    },\n333\t    \"tables\": [\n334\t      \"Table 8: Post-hoc vs OntoCoDec. Reviewer 在 F1 列画箭头：'Post-hoc wins on F1 — the standard metric'\"\n335\t    ],\n336\t    \"figures\": [],\n337\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1 是 worst 档 \\\"method is not state-of-the-art even against trivial baselines\\\" 的核心论据。审稿人不会深入 multi-dimensional framing—— 在 review 时间压力下，\\\"F1 lower than baseline\\\" 是最容易写的 weakness。 Path A reframe 可绕过：如果 Violation Landscape 是主贡献，OntoCoDec 降级为 \\\"one possible mitigation\\\"，则 F1 对比变为 \\\"different approaches in the mitigation space\\\" 而非 \\\"our method vs baseline\\\"。Path B reframe 下 post-hoc 成为 trade-off space 的另一个点。\\n\\n\\nPost-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36; DocRED 9.61 vs 8.23）。 worst 档审稿人直接采取最简解读：(1) \\\"Post-hoc filtering is simpler AND achieves higher F1 on both datasets. The paper's multi-dimensional defense (recall, coverage, operational) is an elaborate way to avoid admitting that a trivial baseline outperforms the proposed method on the standard metric.\\\" (2) \\\"The 'information coverage' argument (DocRED post-hoc discards 48.1%) is misleading — those discarded triples are overwhelmingly incorrect (precision goes from 6.55% to 11.22%). Discarding bad predictions is a feature, not a bug.\\\" (3) \\\"The 'recall preservation' argument (OntoCoDec recall higher) obscures that OntoCoDec's extra recall comes with much lower precision. In low-F1 regimes, precision matters more because most predictions are already wrong.\\\" (4) \\\"Operational advantage (streaming) is an engineering concern, not a research contribution.\\\" 2-3 位审稿人将 post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1 简写为 \\\"post-hoc is strictly better\\\" 并在 weakness 中直接引用这个数字。\\n\"\n338\t  },\n339\t  {\n340\t    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\",\n341\t    \"description\": \"Bootstrap 置信区间检验 F1 变化显著性\",\n342\t    \"results\": {\n343\t      \"scierc_rel_f1_delta_pp\": 0.13,\n344\t      \"scierc_rel_f1_p_value\": 0.58,\n345\t      \"scierc_ent_f1_delta_pp\": -0.03,\n346\t      \"scierc_ent_f1_p_value\": 0.53,\n347\t      \"docred_rel_f1_delta_pp\": 0.5,\n348\t      \"docred_rel_f1_p_value\": 0.001,\n349\t      \"docred_rel_f1_ci_lower\": 0.23,\n350\t      \"docred_rel_f1_ci_upper\": 0.81,\n351\t      \"docred_ent_f1_delta_pp\": 1.23,\n352\t      \"docred_ent_f1_p_value\": 0.001,\n353\t      \"docred_ent_f1_ci_lower\": 0.94,\n354\t      \"docred_ent_f1_ci_upper\": 1.55\n355\t    },\n356\t    \"tables\": [\n357\t      \"Table 9: Bootstrap CI results. Reviewer：'statistically correct but practically meaningless at 8% F1'\"\n358\t    ],\n359\t    \"figures\": [],\n360\t    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap CI 在 worst 档下从 \\\"rigorous evidence\\\" 被降级为 \\\"correctly measured irrelevant effect\\\"。 审稿人论证：(a) SciERC 不显著所以不能声称 F1 中性；(b) DocRED 显著但效果来自 grammar（非 novel）； (c) 绝对 F1 太低，统计显著的微小改善无实际意义。三条攻击互相支撑。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 的统计功在 worst 档下被弱化：(1) \\\"SciERC p=0.58 — F1 change is indistinguishable from noise. You cannot claim F1-neutral either; the CI includes both positive and negative values, so you simply don't know the F1 impact on SciERC.\\\" (2) \\\"DocRED p<0.001 is driven entirely by grammar eliminating OOV names — you showed this yourself (grammar_only E-F1≈full_s1 E-F1). The significant F1 improvement is a grammar artifact, not a constraint enforcement contribution.\\\" (3) \\\"Bootstrap CI on the 8% R-F1 scale — a 0.50pp improvement on a base of 7.74% is +6.5% relative, but in absolute terms the system still extracts almost nothing correctly. Statistical significance ≠ practical significance.\\\" 审稿人承认统计方法正确，但 dismiss practical relevance。\\n\"\n361\t  },\n362\t  {\n363\t    \"name\": \"DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\",\n364\t    \"description\": \"DocRED schema-informed 二次运行（已终止，被 P004 supersede）\",\n365\t    \"results\": {\n366\t      \"status\": \"killed\",\n367\t      \"note\": \"superseded by P004\"\n368\t    },\n369\t    \"tables\": [],\n370\t    \"figures\": [],\n371\t    \"analysis\": \"无影响。确保论文和 supplementary 中无 P020 残留引用即可。\\n\\n实验被终止，无数据产出。worst 档下无独立攻击面，但审稿人如果看到 experiment plan 中 有 killed 实验可能会问 \\\"why was this run killed? was there a methodological issue that required re-running?\\\"——需要在 supplementary material 中简要说明是 pipeline 重构导致的重跑，非数据问题。\\n\"\n372\t  }\n373\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5aa5299-835c-4548-89c8-1d5691e096a5","uuid":"7b2e2ed8-e9ff-4b96-a537-8bc6d6584799","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:19:53.764Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T205155/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 SciERC 上 zero-shot 最小提示下的 ontology violation 基准测试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1724,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.154,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.014,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.01\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: SciERC Phase 0 per-relation violation rates (7 relations). Reviewer 标注：'3 relations drive all violations — this is a data sparsity issue, not a systematic phenomenon'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"审稿人将 violation landscape 从 \\\"systematic phenomenon\\\" 降级为 \\\"long-tail artifact on a small ontology\\\"。 核心攻击：SciERC 只有 7 relations，violation 集中在 3 个关系上，不足以证明 \\\"LLM IE 系统性地违反 ontology constraints\\\"。 Path A reframe 下可辩护：即使集中在 3 个关系，这些关系的 25-42% violation rate 仍对下游系统产生不可忽视影响。 但需要补充更多 ontology 的 violation landscape 数据才能说服审稿人。\\n\\n\\n数据本身无变化。worst 档下审稿人攻击角度：(1) \\\"15.4% DR on a 7-relation ontology is expected — with only 6 entity types and loose constraints on Used-for (787 triples, 0.76%), the violation rate is inflated by 3 specific relations (Feature-of/Compare/Evaluate-for) that account for 85%+ of violations. This is a long-tail artifact, not a systemic problem.\\\" (2) \\\"R-F1=8.23% 说明模型根本没有学到任务结构， 在一个模型基本不会做的任务上测 violation rate 有什么意义？\\\" (3) 2-3 位审稿人认为 SciERC violation landscape 是 \\\"useful but incremental observation\\\"，不足以支撑独立 contribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 SciERC 上 schema-informed prompting 后的 violation 变化\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.058,\n      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -62.4,\n      \"total_triples\": 1661,\n      \"evaluate_for_dr_delta_pp\": 5.8,\n      \"feature_of_dr_delta_pp\": -22.3,\n      \"compare_dr_delta_pp\": -14.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Schema-informed vs minimal per-relation DR delta. Reviewer 圈出：'5/7 relations improve — this is a reasonable success rate for zero-cost intervention'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"\\\"Prompt insufficiency\\\" claim 在 worst 档下被判定 undersupported——审稿人要求至少 3 种 prompting strategy (minimal / schema-informed / few-shot / CoT) 的对比才能声称 \\\"prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable\\\"。 单一 schema-informed prompt 的 62% reduction 反而被用来论证 \\\"prompting works pretty well\\\"。 Path B reframe 可规避：不声称 prompt insufficient，而是将 prompt 定位为 trade-off space 的一个点。\\n\\n\\nworst 档审稿人攻击：(1) \\\"62.4% reduction with just prompting — the problem is largely solvable without constrained decoding. The residual 5.78% could be addressed by better prompt engineering (few-shot, chain-of-thought) rather than building a complex decoding framework.\\\" (2) Evaluate-for regression (+5.8pp) 被 1 位审稿人标记但未被多数视为 critical—— 更致命的是另一角度：\\\"you tested ONE prompting strategy; claiming 'prompt insufficiency' without trying few-shot / CoT / self-consistency is premature.\\\" (3) McNemar test significance 不足以挽回—— 审稿人关注的是 \\\"是否穷尽了 prompt 方案\\\" 而非 \\\"当前方案是否 significant\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 DocRED (96 relations) 上 zero-shot 最小提示下的 violation 基准\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 16540,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.187,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.289,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.075,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.964\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3: DocRED Phase 0 top violations by count/rate. Reviewer：'P31_instance_of DR=60.4% with 533 triples — this single relation type drives the narrative'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"审稿人攻击核心：在 zero-shot R-F1 < 10% 的 setting 下，violation pattern 的外部效度存疑。 \\\"You're characterizing the error patterns of a system that doesn't work\\\" 是最致命的一句。 这直接威胁 C1 (violation landscape) 作为独立贡献的可信度。Path A reframe 需要在论文中前置 \\\"we study violation patterns as a function of ontology structure, not model capability\\\" 的定位， 但审稿人可能仍不买账。\\n\\n\\nworst 档审稿人关注点转移：(1) \\\"RV=28.9% means nearly 1/3 of predicted relations are OOV — the model is barely following instructions. Measuring DR on a system that can't even produce valid relation names is questionable methodology.\\\" (2) \\\"ET=7.5% further confirms the model is struggling with basic task understanding in zero-shot DocRED. Your violation landscape is measuring noise, not systematic behavior.\\\" (3) 1 位审稿人直接质疑：\\\"with 96 relations and no training data, this is a toy evaluation that tells us nothing about how real IE systems would behave.\\\" 核心问题： zero-shot F1 太低 → 审稿人不信 violation pattern 反映真实 IE 系统行为。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B 在 DocRED 上 schema-informed prompting 后的 violation 变化\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.128,\n      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -32,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.945,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.184\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: SciERC vs DocRED prompt effect comparison. Reviewer：'the gap (62% vs 32%) could simply reflect prompt sensitivity to ontology size, not a fundamental limitation'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"32% vs 62% 的 gap 本意支持 \\\"prompt scales poorly\\\" claim，但审稿人反转论证为 \\\"这说明 zero-shot 96-relation 任务太难，不是一个合理的 evaluation setting\\\"。 核心矛盾：作者需要 DocRED 来展示 ontology complexity effect，但 zero-shot DocRED 的质量太低导致审稿人质疑整个 evaluation framework。\\n\\n\\n审稿人攻击点：(1) \\\"Only 32% DR reduction (vs SciERC 62%) — schema-informed prompting degrades with ontology complexity. But wait, you claim this SUPPORTS your method. If prompting scales poorly, surely constrained decoding will also face scalability challenges with 96 relations?\\\" (2) \\\"RV 只从 28.9% 降到 18.4%——prompting 甚至不能解决 OOV 问题，说明模型在 DocRED 上 根本不遵循 instructions。这是模型问题，不是 prompting vs decoding 问题。\\\" (3) parse rate 从 96.4% 降到 94.5%——\\\"prompting actually made parsing slightly worse。\\\" 审稿人用这组数据论证 \\\"zero-shot DocRED 太难，方法无法在此 setting 下有效评估\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Phase 2 SciERC unconstrained 基准（与 Phase 0 一致性验证）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.154,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.014,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.01,\n      \"total_triples\": 1724\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: SciERC ablation matrix (5 configs). Reviewer 在 header 批注：'All R-F1 < 9% — these results are within noise'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"基准实验本身无问题。审稿人利用低绝对 F1 质疑整个实验矩阵的信息量。 \\\"You've shown your method works on bad predictions. Who cares?\\\" 是最简洁的攻击。\\n\\n\\n基准数字与 P001 一致，确认 Phase 2 pipeline 可复现。worst 档下审稿人不攻击一致性， 而是攻击 baseline 本身：\\\"R-F1=8.23% — the model is essentially random. Evaluating constraint enforcement on random-quality output is methodologically questionable.\\\" 这个攻击贯穿所有后续 SciERC 实验——审稿人认为低 F1 下的 violation reduction 没有实际意义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC grammar-only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅 grammar 层（XGrammar CFG）约束下的 SciERC 结果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.148,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 30.98\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Grammar-only 的作用（消除 RV/ET）被审稿人最小化——\\\"this is standard XGrammar application, not a contribution\\\"。同时 grammar-only DR≈unconstrained 成为审稿人论证 \\\"grammar 层 对核心 violation 类型无效\\\" 的证据。在 worst 档下，grammar 层的正面贡献（enabling semantic） 被忽视，只看到 \\\"grammar alone doesn't solve DR\\\"。\\n\\n\\nGrammar 层消除 RV 和 ET 但不影响 DR（14.84% ≈ 15.37%），符合预期——CFG 无法表达 cross-field 约束。worst 档审稿人攻击：(1) \\\"Grammar-only already achieves the main practical benefit — eliminating OOV relation names and invalid entity types. The residual DR=14.84% could be addressed by post-hoc filtering without the complexity of a stateful semantic layer.\\\" (2) \\\"F1 完全不变 (8.23→8.23)——grammar 约束对 extraction quality 零影响。\\\" 审稿人论证 grammar-only 已经 \\\"good enough\\\"，semantic 层的复杂性不值得。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC semantic-only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅 semantic 层（logit masking）约束下的 SciERC 结果\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.117,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.015,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.027,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.15,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.01\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 是 worst 档最危险的数据点之一——它直接暴露了 \\\"如果剥离 XGrammar（已有工具）， 作者的实际贡献只有 24% DR reduction + 引入 2.7% CF\\\"。审稿人会写： \\\"The authors' genuinely novel contribution — the semantic constraint layer — achieves modest violation reduction (24%) while introducing a new type of inconsistency (CF 2.7%).\\\"\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR=11.65%（仅↓24%）——因为没有 grammar 层，遇到 OOV relation 时 semantic 无法查 constraint table，大量 token 位置约束失效。worst 档审稿人攻击： (1) \\\"Semantic-only 24% reduction vs full 94% — this shows your semantic layer is heavily dependent on grammar. But the grammar layer is just XGrammar (existing tool). So your actual novel contribution (semantic layer) only achieves 24% DR reduction on its own.\\\" (2) \\\"CF 已经从 0.08% 跳到 2.71%——semantic 层引入 CF 的同时只减少 24% DR， cost-benefit 不佳。\\\" (3) \\\"R-F1 下降 0.08pp——虽然不显著，但方向是负的。\\\" 这组数据被审稿人用来论证 \\\"核心 novelty（semantic layer）alone 效果不够\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"SciERC grammar+semantic S1 单遍完整约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.009,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.099,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.36,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 30.98,\n      \"total_triples\": 1729\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 (full ablation): Reviewer 在 full_s1 行用红笔标注 CF=9.9%，批注 'new violation introduced by method'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CF=9.9% 是 worst 档的核心 rejection 理由。审稿人不接受 \\\"DR=hard constraint, CF=soft preference\\\" 的分级叙事——认为这是作者为掩盖方法缺陷而设的 ad hoc 区分。\\\"Net violation improvement\\\" 视角 下效果大打折扣。Path B reframe（将 CF 升级为 core research question）可直接应对这一攻击。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.93%（↓94%）是论文核心数字。worst 档审稿人承认 DR reduction 显著，但攻击焦点 转向 CF=9.9%：(1) \\\"You traded 15.37% DR for 9.9% CF. DR violations produce structurally invalid triples; CF violations produce semantically inconsistent entity typing across relations. Both are problematic for downstream systems. The net reduction in 'problematic triples' is only ~5pp, not the claimed 94%.\\\" (2) \\\"CF=9.9% 意味着近 10% 的 entity 在不同 relation 中 被分配了不同 type——这在知识图谱中是致命的一致性问题。作者试图用 'severity distinction' (DR=hard, CF=soft) 来淡化，但这个区分是 subjective 的。\\\" (3) \\\"R-F1 从 8.23 到 8.36 (+0.13pp, p=0.58)——统计不显著，F1 claims 站不住。\\\" (4) 1-2 位审稿人直接引用 CF 数据判定 \\\"method introduces a new violation type to fix another\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC full S2 (ablation)\",\n    \"description\": \"SciERC 两遍 S2 策略 ablation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.01,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.08,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.03,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 31.9,\n      \"total_triples\": 1644,\n      \"total_entities\": 2228\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 S2 行: Reviewer 批注 'S2 was supposed to mitigate CF — it doesn't'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"S2 失败是 worst 档 CF narrative 的加速器。审稿人逻辑：如果连作者自己设计的 CF 缓解策略 都失败了，那 \\\"future work: global consistency pass\\\" 的承诺 credibility 极低。 这将 CF 从 \\\"acknowledged limitation with clear path forward\\\" 降级为 \\\"fundamental unresolved problem that the authors have already failed to address\\\"。\\n\\n\\nS2 设计初衷是用两遍解码缓解 CF，但实际 CF=8.03% vs S1=9.9%——差距不显著（1.87pp）。 worst 档审稿人攻击：(1) \\\"S2 adds significant complexity (two-pass decoding) for negligible CF reduction (-1.87pp). R-F1 actually drops (8.03 vs 8.36). This undermines the authors' ability to iterate on the CF problem — their own best idea for addressing CF failed.\\\" (2) \\\"S2 generates 85 fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) and 246 fewer entities (2228 vs 2474)—— two-pass decoding causes information loss.\\\" (3) \\\"如果作者自己的 S2 方案都解决不了 CF， 这说明 CF 是 per-relation enforcement 的固有缺陷，不是 'future work' 能解决的。\\\" S2 的失败强化了 CF 作为 fundamental limitation 的判定。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B DocRED unconstrained 基准\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.185,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.297,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.025,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 7.74,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 58.15,\n      \"total_triples\": 17497,\n      \"parse_failures\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6: DocRED ablation matrix. Reviewer 在 baseline 行标注 'RV=29.7% — model doesn't understand the task'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RV=29.7% 是 worst 档 DocRED 叙事的核心弱点——审稿人论证 grammar 层的 F1 提升（P010/P012） 只是将 OOV 强制映射到有效关系名，不是真正的 extraction quality 提升。 \\\"Your grammar layer is doing label correction, not constraint enforcement\\\" 是最致命的 reframing。\\n\\n\\nDocRED baseline 暴露两个 worst 档攻击面：(1) RV=29.66%——\\\"nearly 1/3 of triples use non-existent relation names. This is not a violation problem, this is a task comprehension problem. Your method's DR reduction is inflated because grammar forces OOV relations into valid names, artificially improving DR without improving extraction.\\\" (2) R-F1=7.74%—— \\\"absolute quality indistinguishable from noise on a 96-relation task.\\\" 审稿人论证 zero-shot DocRED 不是一个 meaningful evaluation setting。Entity F1=58.15% 被忽视—— \\\"entity extraction is easier, but the paper claims contributions to relation extraction.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED grammar-only\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 grammar 层约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.262,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.31,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 59.38,\n      \"parse_failures\": 13\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6 grammar-only 行：Reviewer 用红色标注 DR↑ 箭头：'grammar makes DR WORSE'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED grammar-only DR 上升是 worst 档最直观的攻击素材。审稿人叙事： \\\"Step 1 of your method (grammar) actively worsens the violation you claim to solve (DR). You need Step 2 (semantic) to clean up the mess Step 1 created. This is not 'composable' constraint enforcement — this is one layer creating problems for another layer to fix.\\\" 这直接挑战 \\\"complementary with enabling dependency\\\" 的技术叙事。\\n\\n\\nGrammar 消除 RV（29.66%→0.03%）和 ET（2.48%→0%），但 DR 从 18.46% 升至 26.17%—— worst 档审稿人抓住这一点：(1) \\\"Grammar INCREASES DR by 7.7pp! When you force OOV relation names into valid names, you're creating new DR violations because the forced valid name has different domain/range constraints than what the model intended. Your grammar layer actively worsens the core problem you claim to solve.\\\" (2) \\\"E-F1 提升 (+1.23pp) 来自消除 OOV entity types——this is not 'constraint enforcement improving extraction,' it's grammar fixing the model's formatting errors. Any JSON schema validator could do this.\\\" (3) \\\"DR=26.17% 是所有配置中最高的——grammar 单独使用 比不用更差。\\\" 审稿人用 grammar-only DR 上升来质疑整个 composable 框架的设计合理性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED semantic-only\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED 仅 semantic 层约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.138,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.299,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.042,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.011,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 7.7,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 57.81\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED semantic-only 数据在 worst 档下被解读为 \\\"作者的核心贡献（semantic 层）在复杂 ontology 上效果有限\\\"。DR 仅降 25%、CF 开始出现、F1 略降——三面夹击。 审稿人在此处建立 \\\"method doesn't scale to complex ontologies\\\" 的论据基础。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR=13.84%（仅↓25%），RV/ET 不变——因为 semantic 层不处理 vocabulary。 worst 档审稿人用这组数据闭合论证：(1) \\\"Semantic-only reduces DR by only 25% while introducing CF=1.05%. Grammar-only increases DR by 42% while fixing RV/ET. Neither layer works well alone. The 'composable' claim is misleading — the layers are CODEPENDENT, and the codependency is fragile (see DocRED fallback rate ~57/doc).\\\" (2) \\\"E-F1 实际下降 0.34pp (57.81 vs 58.15)——semantic 层 alone 对 extraction 有害。\\\" (3) \\\"比较 semantic-only DR=13.84% 和 full_s1 DR=10.21%——加了 grammar 后 DR 只额外 降了 3.6pp。如果 grammar 层 'enables' semantic，为什么 full_s1 DR 不接近 0%？\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED grammar+semantic S1 完整约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.102,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.026,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 8.23,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 59.37,\n      \"parse_failures\": 11\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6 full_s1 行: Reviewer 批注 'DR=10.2% is far from near-complete'\",\n      \"Cross-dataset comparison: SciERC DR↓94% vs DocRED DR↓45%. Reviewer：'this is a 2× degradation, not graceful scaling'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED DR↓44.7% 是 worst 档第二大 rejection driver（仅次于 CF）。审稿人叙事： \\\"The method's flagship claim — near-complete type validity — holds only on a tiny 7-relation ontology. On a realistic 96-relation ontology, 10% of triples remain invalid. Combined with CF=2.57% (new violations introduced), the net violation picture is: 10.2% DR + 2.6% CF = ~12.8% problematic triples, vs baseline 18.5% — a modest 31% net improvement, not the claimed 94%.\\\" 这个 \\\"net improvement\\\" reframing 极其危险。\\n\\n\\nDR=10.21%（↓44.7%）——远低于 SciERC 的 94%。worst 档审稿人攻击： (1) \\\"DR reduction drops from 94% (SciERC) to 45% (DocRED). The method HALVES in effectiveness on a more complex ontology. This is a critical scalability failure — real-world IE ontologies have hundreds of relation types.\\\" (2) \\\"Residual DR=10.21% — every 10th triple still violates domain/range constraints. 'Near-complete' in the title is inaccurate for DocRED.\\\" (3) \\\"Qwen DocRED DR↓44.7% 与 Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% 的巨大差距说明方法效果 高度 model-dependent，不是 ontology-agnostic 的 general solution。\\\" (4) \\\"F1 提升 (+0.50pp R-F1, p<0.001) 主要来自 grammar 消除 OOV—— grammar_only E-F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%。Semantic 层对 F1 零贡献。\\\" 审稿人合并 SciERC 94% vs DocRED 45% 为 \\\"method unreliable on complex scenarios\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC unconstrained\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC unconstrained 基准\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.133,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.006,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.005,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 2.68,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 23.56,\n      \"total_relations\": 1274,\n      \"parse_failures\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7: Cross-model comparison. Reviewer 标注 Llama R-F1 列：'2.68% is noise'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama SciERC baseline 暴露了 cross-model 验证的结构性弱点：两个模型在同一任务上 质量差异巨大（2.68% vs 8.23%），说明 zero-shot IE 本身不稳定。审稿人论证 \\\"if the base task quality varies 3× across models, constraint enforcement on top of it is evaluating a moving target\\\"。\\n\\n\\nLlama SciERC R-F1=2.68%——比 Qwen 的 8.23% 还低 3×。worst 档审稿人攻击： (1) \\\"R-F1=2.68% — this model extracts essentially nothing correct. Demonstrating constraint enforcement on a model with 2.68% F1 is meaningless.\\\" (2) \\\"You chose Llama specifically because it has low RV (0.55%) — this makes grammar layer look good (it has nothing to fix). But the real story is the model can't do the task.\\\" (3) \\\"E-F1=23.56% (vs Qwen 31.01%)—— Llama 在 SciERC 上全面弱于 Qwen，cross-model 'validation' 只是在一个更弱的模型上 重复了同样的实验。\\\" 审稿人认为 2 个 8B 模型 + 2 个数据集 = 最低限度验证，不足以 支撑 generalization claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC 完整 S1 约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.066,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 2.54,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 23.49,\n      \"total_relations\": 1315\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 Llama S1 行: Reviewer 标注 CF=6.56% + R-F1↓\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama SciERC DR↓99.4% 表面极好但审稿人论证这是 \\\"easy case\\\"（低 RV baseline）。 CF=6.56% 高于 Qwen 同场景进一步支持 \\\"CF is model-dependent and unpredictable\\\" 叙事。 R-F1 下降虽小但方向不利——\\\"constrained decoding hurts already-weak models\\\" 的论点。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.08%（↓99.4%）——数字极好，但 worst 档审稿人翻转叙事： (1) \\\"DR↓99.4% on Llama vs ↓94% on Qwen — why does the method work BETTER on the weaker model? Because Llama has near-zero RV (0.55%), so grammar layer encounters fewer OOV issues and semantic layer operates more cleanly. This means your method's effectiveness depends heavily on the model's baseline vocabulary compliance, not on the method's own capability.\\\" (2) \\\"CF=6.56% — higher than Qwen's CF rate on the same dataset. Constrained decoding destabilizes Llama's entity typing more than Qwen's.\\\" (3) \\\"R-F1 从 2.68% 降到 2.54% (-0.14pp)——在已经极低的 F1 上还进一步下降。\\\" (4) \\\"Parse failure 从 1 增加到... 好吧 Llama SciERC parse failure 没增加， 但 R-F1 下降 + CF 升高 = constrained decoding hurts Llama stability。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED unconstrained\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED unconstrained 基准\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.261,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.16,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 5.98,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 55.65,\n      \"parse_failures\": 68,\n      \"documents_checked\": 930\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 Llama DocRED baseline: Reviewer：'68 parse failures (6.8%) — significant selection bias'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED baseline 的 parse failure=6.8% 引入 selection bias 攻击。审稿人指出： checker 跳过 parse failures → F1 只在成功解析的 93.2% 样本上计算 → 这些样本可能 系统性地 easier/better → 所有 Llama DocRED 数字都有上偏。 虽然偏差方向对 constrained decoding 不利（见 P016 parse failure 更高）， 但审稿人可能不接受这个辩护——\\\"you should report F1 on ALL documents, with parse failures counted as zero extraction\\\"。\\n\\n\\nParse failures=68/998（6.8%）是 worst 档攻击面之一：(1) \\\"6.8% parse failure rate means the model can't even produce valid JSON 7% of the time. These failures are excluded from F1 calculation — creating a selection bias that favors the method.\\\" (2) \\\"DR=26.07% (vs Qwen 18.46%) — Llama has MORE DR violations on DocRED despite having FEWER RV violations (16.0% vs 29.7%). This contradicts the 'tightness × RV baseline' narrative — if RV explains DR reduction gap, why does Llama have higher baseline DR with lower baseline RV?\\\" 审稿人用这个不一致来质疑 D014 dual-factor 解释。 (3) \\\"R-F1=5.98% — even worse than Qwen's 7.74%. Another data point confirming zero-shot DocRED is not a meaningful evaluation setting.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED 完整 S1 约束\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.026,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.12,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 6.27,\n      \"entity_f1_pct\": 55.01,\n      \"parse_failures\": 91,\n      \"documents_checked\": 907\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 Llama DocRED S1: 被红色标注的数字 — CF=12.02%, parse_failures=91, E-F1↓0.64pp\",\n      \"Cross-model CF comparison: Qwen 2.57% vs Llama 12.02%. Reviewer：'CF is 4.7× worse on Llama — this is not a stable method'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED full_s1 是 worst 档 \\\"方法不稳定\\\" 论据的核心证据。CF=12.02%、 parse_failures 增加 33.8%、E-F1 下降——三个负面指标同时出现。 审稿人叙事总结：\\\"On Llama DocRED, OntoCoDec reduces DR from 26% to 2.5% (good), but introduces CF=12% (new problem), increases parse failures by 34% (stability issue), and slightly degrades entity F1 (quality loss). The trade-off is unfavorable.\\\" 这是 ≥2 审稿人给 reject 的关键段落。\\n\\n\\nDR=2.55%（↓90.2%）——比 Qwen 的 44.7% 好得多，但 worst 档审稿人合并攻击面： (1) \\\"CF=12.02% — the highest of any configuration. One in eight entities has inconsistent typing. On DocRED this is especially problematic because the same entities appear across many relations in a document.\\\" (2) \\\"Parse failures increased from 68 to 91 (+33.8%)—— constrained decoding actively destabilizes Llama's JSON generation. 23 additional documents produced unparseable output BECAUSE of your constraints.\\\" (3) \\\"E-F1=55.01% (↓0.64pp)—— entity extraction quality dropped. This contradicts the SciERC claim of F1-neutrality.\\\" (4) \\\"Cross-model inconsistency: Qwen DR↓44.7% vs Llama DR↓90.2% (2× gap). Method effectiveness varies wildly across models — users cannot predict what reduction they'll get.\\\" (5) \\\"CF 跨模型差异更极端：Qwen CF=2.57% vs Llama CF=12.02% (4.7× gap)。 方法引入的新问题（CF）比它解决的旧问题（DR）更不可预测。\\\" 审稿人合并所有 cross-model 不一致性判定 \\\"method is unreliable\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"S2 pilot (50 docs)\",\n    \"description\": \"S2 两遍策略 50 文档 pilot 测试\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.021,\n      \"relation_f1_pct\": 10.08,\n      \"samples\": 50,\n      \"predicted_relations\": 146\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pilot50 在 worst 档下无独立攻击面，但论文必须确保无残留引用。 审稿人通常会在 Appendix 检查 pilot 数字与主表一致性。\\n\\n\\nPilot50 数据已被全量 S2（P008）supersede。worst 档审稿人会在看到论文引用 pilot50 时 检查是否与全量数据一致——pilot DR=2.05% vs full DR=0.97%，数字不一致。 如果论文任何地方残留 pilot50 数字，审稿人会标注 \\\"inconsistent reporting\\\"。 但因为 pilot 已明确标注为 superseded，主要风险是论文写作中的引用错误。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-hoc filtering baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Post-hoc 过滤 baseline 对比（删除违规 triples）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_f1_after\": 8.63,\n      \"scierc_f1_before\": 8.23,\n      \"scierc_rejection_rate\": 0.168,\n      \"scierc_recall_after\": 10.68,\n      \"scierc_recall_before\": 11.4,\n      \"scierc_tp_before\": 111,\n      \"scierc_tp_after\": 104,\n      \"docred_f1_after\": 9.61,\n      \"docred_f1_before\": 7.74,\n      \"docred_rejection_rate\": 0.481,\n      \"docred_recall_after\": 8.4,\n      \"docred_recall_before\": 9.46,\n      \"docred_tp_before\": 1137,\n      \"docred_tp_after\": 1010,\n      \"docred_et_residual\": 0.025\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: Post-hoc vs OntoCoDec. Reviewer 在 F1 列画箭头：'Post-hoc wins on F1 — the standard metric'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1 是 worst 档 \\\"method is not state-of-the-art even against trivial baselines\\\" 的核心论据。审稿人不会深入 multi-dimensional framing—— 在 review 时间压力下，\\\"F1 lower than baseline\\\" 是最容易写的 weakness。 Path A reframe 可绕过：如果 Violation Landscape 是主贡献，OntoCoDec 降级为 \\\"one possible mitigation\\\"，则 F1 对比变为 \\\"different approaches in the mitigation space\\\" 而非 \\\"our method vs baseline\\\"。Path B reframe 下 post-hoc 成为 trade-off space 的另一个点。\\n\\n\\nPost-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36; DocRED 9.61 vs 8.23）。 worst 档审稿人直接采取最简解读：(1) \\\"Post-hoc filtering is simpler AND achieves higher F1 on both datasets. The paper's multi-dimensional defense (recall, coverage, operational) is an elaborate way to avoid admitting that a trivial baseline outperforms the proposed method on the standard metric.\\\" (2) \\\"The 'information coverage' argument (DocRED post-hoc discards 48.1%) is misleading — those discarded triples are overwhelmingly incorrect (precision goes from 6.55% to 11.22%). Discarding bad predictions is a feature, not a bug.\\\" (3) \\\"The 'recall preservation' argument (OntoCoDec recall higher) obscures that OntoCoDec's extra recall comes with much lower precision. In low-F1 regimes, precision matters more because most predictions are already wrong.\\\" (4) \\\"Operational advantage (streaming) is an engineering concern, not a research contribution.\\\" 2-3 位审稿人将 post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1 简写为 \\\"post-hoc is strictly better\\\" 并在 weakness 中直接引用这个数字。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\",\n    \"description\": \"Bootstrap 置信区间检验 F1 变化显著性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_rel_f1_delta_pp\": 0.13,\n      \"scierc_rel_f1_p_value\": 0.58,\n      \"scierc_ent_f1_delta_pp\": -0.03,\n      \"scierc_ent_f1_p_value\": 0.53,\n      \"docred_rel_f1_delta_pp\": 0.5,\n      \"docred_rel_f1_p_value\": 0.001,\n      \"docred_rel_f1_ci_lower\": 0.23,\n      \"docred_rel_f1_ci_upper\": 0.81,\n      \"docred_ent_f1_delta_pp\": 1.23,\n      \"docred_ent_f1_p_value\": 0.001,\n      \"docred_ent_f1_ci_lower\": 0.94,\n      \"docred_ent_f1_ci_upper\": 1.55\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 9: Bootstrap CI results. Reviewer：'statistically correct but practically meaningless at 8% F1'\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap CI 在 worst 档下从 \\\"rigorous evidence\\\" 被降级为 \\\"correctly measured irrelevant effect\\\"。 审稿人论证：(a) SciERC 不显著所以不能声称 F1 中性；(b) DocRED 显著但效果来自 grammar（非 novel）； (c) 绝对 F1 太低，统计显著的微小改善无实际意义。三条攻击互相支撑。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 的统计功在 worst 档下被弱化：(1) \\\"SciERC p=0.58 — F1 change is indistinguishable from noise. You cannot claim F1-neutral either; the CI includes both positive and negative values, so you simply don't know the F1 impact on SciERC.\\\" (2) \\\"DocRED p<0.001 is driven entirely by grammar eliminating OOV names — you showed this yourself (grammar_only E-F1≈full_s1 E-F1). The significant F1 improvement is a grammar artifact, not a constraint enforcement contribution.\\\" (3) \\\"Bootstrap CI on the 8% R-F1 scale — a 0.50pp improvement on a base of 7.74% is +6.5% relative, but in absolute terms the system still extracts almost nothing correctly. Statistical significance ≠ practical significance.\\\" 审稿人承认统计方法正确，但 dismiss practical relevance。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED schema-informed 二次运行（已终止，被 P004 supersede）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\",\n      \"note\": \"superseded by P004\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"无影响。确保论文和 supplementary 中无 P020 残留引用即可。\\n\\n实验被终止，无数据产出。worst 档下无独立攻击面，但审稿人如果看到 experiment plan 中 有 killed 实验可能会问 \\\"why was this run killed? was there a methodological issue that required re-running?\\\"——需要在 supplementary material 中简要说明是 pipeline 重构导致的重跑，非数据问题。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":373,"startLine":1,"totalLines":373}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T4hfRiipcUzVPHbXA67of8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n12\t\n13\t**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n14\t- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n15\t- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n16\t- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n17\t- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n18\t\n19\t## Core Claims\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n22\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n23\t\n24\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n25\t\n26\t**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n27\t\n28\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n31\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n32\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n33\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n34\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n35\t\n36\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n37\t\n38\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n39\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n40\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n41\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n42\t\n43\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n44\t\n45\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n46\t\n47\t**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\n48\tWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n49\t\n50\t**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n51\t- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n52\t- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n53\t- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n54\t- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n55\t\n56\t**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n57\t\n58\t**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n59\t\n60\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n61\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n62\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n63\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n64\t\n65\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n66\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n67\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n68\t\n69\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n70\t\n71\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n72\t\n73\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n74\t\n75\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n76\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n77\t\n78\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n79\t**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n80\t\n81\tPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n82\t\n83\t**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n84\t1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n85\t2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n86\t3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n87\t4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n88\t\n89\t数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n90\t\n91\t**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n92\t5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n93\t6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n94\t7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n95\t\n96\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n97\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n98\t\n99\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n100\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n101\t\n102\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n103\t\n104\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n105\t**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE. Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n106\t- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), F1-neutral (-0.14pp)\n107\t- DocRED unconstrained: DR 26.15%, RV 16.03%, R-F1 5.98% (parse failures 6.8% vs Qwen 1.2%)\n108\t- DocRED full_s1: 🔄 ETA ~20:19 UTC\n109\t\n110\t**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n111\t- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n112\t- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n113\t- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n114\t- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n115\t- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n116\t- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n117\t\n118\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n119\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **D012 Bootstrap CI (10000×, v2 fix) 结果**:\n120\t- SciERC: Rel F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58), Ent F1 -0.03pp (p=0.53) → **F1-neutral**\n121\t- DocRED: Rel F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.23, +0.81]), Ent F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.94, +1.55]) → **双双显著提升**\n122\t- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n123\t- Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement preserves or improves extraction quality: F1-neutral on SciERC; statistically significant Rel F1 and Entity F1 improvement on DocRED (p<0.001).\"\n124\t- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告 significance + 机制归因。Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n125\t\n126\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n127\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n128\t\n129\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n130\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n131\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n132\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n133\t\n134\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n135\t\n136\t**论证层次**：\n137\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n138\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n139\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n140\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n141\t\n142\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n143\t\n144\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n145\t\n146\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n147\t\n148\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n149\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n150\t\n151\t## Paper Structure (Draft)\n152\t1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n153\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n154\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n155\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n156\t5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n157\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n158\t7. Conclusion\n159\t\n160\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n161\t\n162\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n163\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n164\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n165\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n166\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n167\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n168\t\n169\t**Claim with caution**:\n170\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n171\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n172\t- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n173\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n174\t\n175\t**Do NOT claim**:\n176\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n177\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n178\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n179\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n180\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n181\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n182\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n183\t\n184\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n185\t\n186\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n187\t2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n188\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n189\t4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n190\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n191\t\n192\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n193\t\n194\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n195\t- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n196\t- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n197\t- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n198\t- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n199\t- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n200\t- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n201\t\n202\t**当前瓶颈**: D014 论文修订（tightness claim + cross-model subsection + E-F1 claim limitation）\n203\t\n204\t## Status\n205\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n206\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n207\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n208\t- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n209\t- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n210\t- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n211\t- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n212\t- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n213\t- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n214\t- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n215\t- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n216\t- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n217\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n218\t- D014 tightness revision: 🔄 Agent executing (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n219\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f5aa5299-835c-4548-89c8-1d5691e096a5","uuid":"ecdab67f-a1c8-4a6b-bc71-64f788fa139e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:19:53.770Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T205155/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\nWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n\n**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n\n**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n\n**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n\nPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n\n**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n\n数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n\n**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE. Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), F1-neutral (-0.14pp)\n- DocRED unconstrained: DR 26.15%, RV 16.03%, R-F1 5.98% (parse failures 6.8% vs Qwen 1.2%)\n- DocRED full_s1: 🔄 ETA ~20:19 UTC\n\n**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **D012 Bootstrap CI (10000×, v2 fix) 结果**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58), Ent F1 -0.03pp (p=0.53) → **F1-neutral**\n- DocRED: Rel F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.23, +0.81]), Ent F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.94, +1.55]) → **双双显著提升**\n- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n- Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement preserves or improves extraction quality: F1-neutral on SciERC; statistically significant Rel F1 and Entity F1 improvement on DocRED (p<0.001).\"\n- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告 significance + 机制归因。Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n7. Conclusion\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n\n**当前瓶颈**: D014 论文修订（tightness claim + cross-model subsection + E-F1 claim limitation）\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n- D014 tightness revision: 🔄 Agent executing (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n","numLines":219,"startLine":1,"totalLines":219}}}
